392
00:51:03.950 --> 00:51:10.890
lightclient: this idea that Vitalik had around having a stark, verification of the EVM execution in the frame.

393
00:51:11.280 --> 00:51:21.200
lightclient: To me, like, I think that we should be planning for signature aggregation without the assumption that there's any kind of, like, EVM, you know, stark proof.

394
00:51:22.500 --> 00:51:28.410
lightclient: like… This technology is obviously… Improving rapidly?

395
00:51:28.740 --> 00:51:29.720
lightclient: But…

396
00:51:31.210 --> 00:51:45.389
lightclient: bringing that into the core protocol is going to be a very big challenge, and I think signature aggregation is something that we understand much more deeply, and something that's much more likely to land in the near future.

397
00:51:45.620 --> 00:51:49.990
lightclient: I also think that, like, for post-quantum, we really can't gamble on…

398
00:51:51.120 --> 00:52:00.989
lightclient: you know, assuming that ZK EVM will exist, that we can ship into the Layer 1 protocol to do this signature aggregation. I think that, like, in the farther future, it's…

399
00:52:01.210 --> 00:52:05.689
lightclient: You know, a very good, possibility.

400
00:52:05.970 --> 00:52:12.040
lightclient: Very likely possibility, especially for the types of signatures that we don't necessarily understand.

401
00:52:12.370 --> 00:52:23.969
lightclient: I think that's, like, a good place for it. But for this type of signatures that we do understand, that we, you know, very likely will be aggregating when we start introducing, I suppose, quantum, crypto.

402
00:52:26.310 --> 00:52:39.340
lightclient: We need 8288 for PQ private transactions. Yeah, I mean, we need this for PQ private transactions, and when this technology is ready,

403
00:52:39.570 --> 00:52:44.100
